# Build context is the repo root (docker-compose.yml build.context: ../..)
# since the Dockerfile builds admin-portal + bot-ui + ai-search-engine into
# one image (docs/SINGLE_ORIGIN_DEPLOY.md).
#
# Every pattern below is **/-prefixed to match at ANY depth unambiguously -
# a bare pattern like "node_modules/" was tried first and did NOT exclude
# admin-portal/node_modules or bot-ui/node_modules (verified: build context
# was 2.72GB, matching the on-disk size of node_modules+.next+venv combined,
# meaning none of it was actually filtered). Also listed by exact path as a
# second safety net.

# Backend: only requirements.txt, app/, config/, scripts/ are ever COPYed.
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
ai-search-engine/venv/
ai-search-engine/evals/
ai-search-engine/loadtest/
ai-search-engine/tests/

# Frontends: only the source the Dockerfile's npm ci/build stage needs -
# node_modules and prior build output are regenerated inside the image, not
# reused from the host, and are typically the largest thing here.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
admin-portal/node_modules/
admin-portal/.next/
bot-ui/node_modules/
bot-ui/.next/

# Never meant to reach an image, regardless of directory.
docs/
**/*.log
.git/
*.png

# Only the BACKEND's real secrets file is excluded. admin-portal/.env.local
# and bot-ui/.env.local contain NEXT_PUBLIC_* values ONLY - inherently public
# (they're baked straight into the browser JS bundle by design, e.g. the
# Entra client_id) - and MUST reach `next build`, or Next.js silently inlines
# empty strings for them. A blanket **/.env* pattern here previously did
# exactly that: verified the built admin-portal JS had `clientId:""`, which
# is why MSAL sign-in failed with AADSTS900144 (missing client_id).
ai-search-engine/.env

# IDE/editor cruft.
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
